  "about": "What shopkeepers make now (doc 35, Phase 5, first part). Each craft is a whole batch from at most two ingredients, every ingredient sold by a supplying shop in town (supplies). makers: the businesses (businesses.json) whose keepers make it. seconds: game seconds of work for one batch. A shopkeeper makes nothing from nothing: a batch takes its ingredients from the keeper's own stock, bought from a supplier when it runs low. Workshop crafts (flour, linen cloth, leather, cord, butchering) make the suppliers' goods from what producers bring in. producers: residents whose work label holds one of `match` turn a spell of work (seconds) into `out` from the land (only in `seasons`, 0 spring to 3 winter, if given), keeping a few of each to sell to the town. recipes.json keeps the full chains for later phases.",
